content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-104 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22871, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing vibration is reported as 7.6 mm/s. The applicable criterion is Figure 3 vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. The 7.1–11.0 mm/s range is Zone D, so 7.6 mm/s is above the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary and falls in Zone D: 'Damage likely - stop the pump.' It is not an exact-boundary classification case.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing-housing temperature is 84 C. The applicable housing-surface temperature limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C, and trip at 90 C. Thus 84 C is above normal and 4 C above the alarm level, but below the 90 C trip level. The temperature alone has not reached the documented trip value; immediate stopping is independently required by the Zone D vibration classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-area leakage is approximately one drop per second. No numerical allowable drip rate is documented in the supplied evidence. The applicable troubleshooting entry is 'Leakage at shaft seal,' which directs mechanical-seal replacement under 5.2 and an alignment check under 5.4; possible causes include worn or cracked seal faces, dry running, and shaft misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported dry run lasted about 10 minutes. The applicable requirement is absolute: seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge and the pump must never run dry. No permissible dry-run duration is provided, so the 10-minute event contradicts that requirement.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Dry-run damage to the mechanical seal, or worn/cracked seal faces, is the leading explanation for the shaft leakage: the reported dry run preceded the work request, dry running is prohibited, and seal run dry is expressly listed as a probable cause of shaft-seal leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment could connect the seal leakage, high vibration, and high bearing temperature because it is listed as a probable cause for all three symptoms. Alignment must therefore be checked rather than attributing the findings to the seal alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear is a possible explanation for the high vibration and high housing temperature. Over-greasing is another documented possible cause of high bearing temperature, so grease quantity must be checked alongside bearing condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation/inadequate NPSH remain alternative documented causes of high vibration. The report does not establish which of these, if any, is present; inspect the impeller and check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-104 immediately and keep it out of service pending repair. The reported 7.6 mm/s bearing-housing vibration is in Figure 3 Zone D, whose specified action is 'Damage likely - stop the pump.'",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump. Use the back pull-out arrangement so the rotating assembly can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework. The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so provide lifting equipment before removal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly, impeller nut, and impeller. Withdraw the seal and sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth; this scoring inspection remains required even though the replacement cartridge seal itself is pre-set.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate the vibration and temperature findings: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings and impeller, and check NPSH. Because high bearing temperature is reported, procedure 5.3 requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows high temperature; install drive-end HF3-512 and non-drive-end HF3-510 together.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit one new HF3-450B cartridge mechanical seal; do not fit HF3-450 on this serial-numbered pump. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket as required by procedure 5.2 and whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble and tighten the HF3-450B seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, not the superseded 25 Nm value for this asset. For the other Table 5 fasteners, with lightly oiled threads, tighten M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm, the M24 impeller nut to 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm where disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Perform laser shaft alignment after the seal and bearing work, and in every case where the motor or bearing housing has been moved. Achieve parallel offset no greater than 0.05 mm and angular misalignment no greater than 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before operating the pump, establish Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and do not run it dry. Reinstate condition monitoring by measuring vibration velocity on both bearing housings every week and classifying the highest reading with Figure 3; measure bearing temperature on the housing surface and apply the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm, and 90 C trip criteria.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C01"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal. Required replacement for HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward, including HF3-22871. Do not substitute HF3-450; glandnut torque is 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; fit a new gasket during seal replacement and replace it whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. This is a conditional replacement part: inspect after withdrawal and replace if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with the non-drive-end bearing under the high-temperature pair-replacement requirement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace as a pair with the drive-end bearing rather than replacing only the hot drive-end bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Shutdown and isolation control: stop the pump for the Zone D vibration condition, then isolate and drain it before seal or bearing disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting control: the back pull-out assembly mass is 68 kg and the specification explicitly requires lifting equipment; arrange suitable lifting equipment before removal.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry-running control: seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge and the pump must never run dry. Establish the flush arrangement before operation and address the changeover practice that allowed the reported dry run.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical control: P-104 is one of the filtered-water-line pumps chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Treat the drained fluid and wetted components as chemically dosed; obtain the site-specific PPE, decontamination, and drainage requirements before opening because those details are not supplied in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement standard allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 8.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing-pair replacement standard allowance: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12.0 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-alignment standard allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician, equivalent to 1.5 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For the planned seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement, and laser alignment, the arithmetic sum of standard task durations is 11.5 hours and total labour content is 21.5 technician-hours. The table does not specify task overlap, additional inspection time, chemical preparation, or delay allowances, so this is not a guaranteed elapsed outage duration.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal selection conflict: the manual parts list identifies HF3-450, a component-type seal, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits fitting HF3-450 on pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and requires pre-set cartridge HF3-450B. P-104 is serial HF3-22871 and therefore falls explicitly within the bulletin range, so HF3-450B governs this repair. The manual is Revision D, but its issue date is not supplied; the explicit serial range resolves applicability without assuming which document is newer.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because this asset is within the bulletin serial range and is receiving HF3-450B, use 30 Nm; 25 Nm is the superseded value for this repair. The other Table 5 fastener torques remain applicable where those fasteners are disturbed.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Confirm that the reported 7.6 mm/s vibration value is vibration velocity in mm/s RMS, and obtain the non-drive-end bearing-housing reading. Figure 3 is an RMS-velocity chart and the manual requires measurement on both housings with classification of the highest reading (C06, C07).",
    "What is the measured shaft-sleeve scoring depth? The sleeve replacement decision depends on whether scoring exceeds 0.1 mm; the pre-set seal's elimination of sleeve measurement for seal setting does not answer this condition question (C10, C13).",
    "What are the actual grease quantity, bearing condition or noise findings, impeller condition, alignment measurements, and NPSH/cavitation findings? These missing observations are needed to distinguish the documented possible causes beyond the strong dry-run/seal-leak association (C09, C10).",
    "What site-specific sodium-hypochlorite PPE, decontamination, isolation-verification, and drained-fluid handling requirements apply? The evidence establishes chemical dosing but provides no concentration or chemical-work procedure (C16).",
    "What numerical shaft-seal leakage acceptance criterion, if any, applies after repair? The supplied troubleshooting guidance directs seal replacement and alignment checking for shaft-seal leakage but gives no allowable drip-rate limit (C09)."
  ]
}
